# Public Android identity, taken from the owner-supplied Android-10 Coral dump.
# Android Q derives the unscoped ro.product.{brand,device,manufacturer,model,
# name} from the first namespace that defines each one, in the default order
# product,product_services,odm,vendor,system
# (system/core/init/property_service.cpp:801, overridable at runtime by
# ro.product.property_source_order). product is first, so these five win; the
# omitted product_services namespace sits between product and odm and this
# device defines nothing there. Structural TARGET_DEVICE/board/platform
# properties remain k50sv1_64_bsp/mt6755 elsewhere in the tree.
ro.product.product.brand=google
ro.product.product.device=coral
ro.product.product.manufacturer=Google
ro.product.product.model=Pixel 4 XL
ro.product.product.name=coral
